# Every text file stays LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# The POSIX installer and both shell suites are line-ending sensitive, the
# installers copy files byte-for-byte, and tests/test_install.ps1 asserts that
# setup.ps1 has no byte above 0x7F (a CR would not fail that, but a CRLF
# checkout of setup.sh would break bash and the LF assertions). Git on the
# authoring machine has core.autocrlf=true, so without this file a Windows
# clone would check the shell scripts out with CRLF.
#
# Windows PowerShell 5.1 and 7 both read LF-only .ps1 files correctly.
* text=auto eol=lf
